#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:44
#: 500467f051644975b1f17e16049ef643
msgid ""
"Some software which is not available in the default Debian repositories can "
"be installed through `extrepo <https://manpages.debian.org/stable/extrepo/"
"extrepo.1p.en.html>`__, a Debian tool for safely managing external "
"repositories. Qubes OS Debian templates ship with ``extrepo`` and ``extrepo-"
"offline-data`` pre-installed and configured for offline use, so you do not "
"need to give the template network access to enable a repository. Use of "
"`extrepo` is documented in the man page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:47
#: 26b5aceb7c1c48c6b087b7fe0908e864
msgid ""
"While the repositories managed by ``extrepo`` are curated by Debian, the "
"Debian project makes no warranty as to the security or quality of the "
"software in these third-party repositories. We recommend that you install "
"third-party software in a dedicated :term:`template` rather than the default "
"one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:50
#: 18595112e9864d1b89e7c3561dfb60dc
msgid ""
"For software packages available from repositories **not** included in "
"extrepo, you must create a repository definition and install the relevant "
"signing key. This will usually be documented by the software provider. The "
"only Qubes specific part is that you will have to download the signing key "
"in an online qube, and then use ``qvm-move`` to transfer the key to your "
"template."
msgstr ""

