msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:238
#: db71eee7e60349209fa8823f36063aa3
msgid ""
"Please see :doc:`How to Reinstall a template </user/how-to-guides/how-to-"
"reinstall-a-template>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:241
#: cd120e8cb5fa4307b645a685ece08645
msgid "Full revert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:243
#: 4bdfa7e7aac0457690f87e669427c9a2
msgid "This is like the simple revert, except:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:245
#: 67b52a316cb447b88cd8c45cdaef0651
msgid ""
"You must also revert the private volume with :samp:`qvm-volume revert "
"{<template>}:private`. This requires you to have an old revision of the "
"private volume, which does not exist with the current default config. "
"However, if you don’t have anything important in the private volume (likely "
"for a template), then you can work around this by just resetting the private "
"volume with :samp:`qvm-volume import --no-resize {<template>}:private /dev/"
"null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:247
#: af212bfda20847a2824cb2c5934b1931
msgid ""
"The saved revision of the volumes must be uncompromised. With the default "
"``revisions_to_keep=1`` for the root volume, you must **not** have started "
"the template since the compromising action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:252
#: 226aef9f11d646de961b0917673c586d
msgid "Updates proxy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:254
#: b99d29a11cae4315bd0d28950b66aef6
msgid ""
"Updates proxy is a service which allows access from package managers "
"configured to use the proxy by default, but can be used by any other program "
"that accepts proxy arguments. The purpose of the proxy, instead of direct "
"network access, is meant to mitigate user errors of using applications such "
"as the browser in the template. Not necessarily what part of the network "
"they can access, but only to applications trusted by the user, configured to "
"use the proxy. The http proxy (tinyproxy) does not filter traffic because it "
"is hard to list all the repository mirrors and keep that list up to date). "
"it also does not cache anything."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:256
#: 9606227597f1401295a2ef35b7212f49
msgid ""
"The proxy is running in selected VMs (by default all the NetVMs (1)) and "
"intercepts traffic directed to 127.0.0.1:8082. Thanks to such configuration "
"all the VMs can use the same proxy address. If the VM is configured to have "
"access to the updates proxy (2), the startup scripts will automatically "
"configure dnf/apt to really use the proxy (3). Also access to updates proxy "
"is independent of any other firewall settings (VM will have access to "
"updates proxy, even if policy is set to block all the traffic)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:258
#: d7d91815ae5a4c8ab4a00b630bb8b42f
msgid ""
"There are two services (``qvm-service``, :doc:`service framework </user/"
"advanced-topics/qubes-service>`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:260
#: be5f9bb4bf6f468487eed0431de8b7f4
msgid ""
"``qubes-updates-proxy`` (and its deprecated name: ``qubes-yum-proxy``) - a "
"service providing a proxy for templates - by default enabled in NetVMs "
"(especially: sys-net)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:262
#: 0d0bab7efdd149f192194d44b4d270f0
msgid ""
"``updates-proxy-setup`` (and its deprecated name: ``yum-proxy-setup``) - use "
"a proxy provided by another VM (instead of downloading updates directly), "
"enabled by default in all templates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:264
#: 1ace090d15e749e998b453d3ab1cd3a8
msgid ""
"Both the old and new names work. The defaults listed above are applied if "
"the service is not explicitly listed in the services tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:267
#: ac8ea7d38a0d432f9df9dc3eccfbe6e2
msgid "Technical details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:269
#: 015523af7151416d8512c77be0185ea9
msgid ""
"The updates proxy uses RPC/qrexec. The proxy is configured in qrexec policy "
"in dom0: ``/etc/qubes/policy.d/90-default.policy``. By default this is set "
"to sys-net and/or sys-whonix, depending on firstboot choices. This new "
"design allows for templates to be updated even when they are not connected "
"to any NetVM."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/how-to-guides/how-to-install-software.rst:271
#: e2269dbb444b4509bcb99ae88e53ccb7
msgid ""
"Example policy file in R4.2 (with Whonix installed, but not set as default "
"UpdateVM for all templates):"
msgstr ""

